<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1297">1297</a>–<a href="/years/1316">1316</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> was a younger son of Duke Robert II of Burgundy who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-hainaut">Matilda of Hainaut</a> and became prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in 1313. He defeated and killed his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-of-majorca">Ferdinand of Majorca</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manolada">Battle of Manolada</a> in 1316, but died shortly after, reportedly of poison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Louis of Burgundy" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schlumberger, Gustave Léon, 1844-1929 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_of_Burgundy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
